<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2016/Millville.jpg" alt="A painting of fields at Millville Road in Upperville VA" width="375" height="486" data-filename="Millville Road.JPG" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Millville Road. 7x5, oil on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">One of the things that I've been working on over the past couple of weeks has been an increased emphasis on abstraction. It's not that I suddenly want to declare myself an abstract painter, I just want to use it as a way to place more emphasis on the light and the shapes. All that comes, of course, at the expense of the representation of forms.</p>